# Provider Reference

Each fact states where it came from. Nothing here is recalled.

## ConnexPay — verified from docs.connexpay.com on 2026-08-20

**`CustomerID`** — accepted on **Auth Only**, **Create Sale**, **Capture**. **Absent** from
**Void** and **Return** request bodies. String, optional, max 100 characters, alphanumeric
plus `[._/-]`.

> "Transaction ID within client environment associated with the customer. This value acts as
> a secondary identifier in conjunction with OrderNumber. The value is searchable and
> reportable in the ConnexPay portal. This value may be sent in multiple times within the
> integration for multiple purposes."

**`Customer` object** — top level, and:

> "Customer Data. This will only be used if TenderType is not Credit"

So the block at `PurchaseRequest.php:132` is correctly sent only on the Cash path
(`visitCash`), and card payments carry identity through `Card.Customer` and `RiskData`
instead. This is already right; do not change it.

**`OrderNumber`** — max 50, alphanumeric plus `[._/-]`. A reporting and reconciliation key,
searchable in Bridge, carried into the Chargeback Management System. **Not** an idempotency
key. Capture's value **overwrites** the Auth's.

**`SequenceNumber`** — max 100 alphanumeric, no specials listed. Duplicate detection, and
only in combination:

> "If a sale request with the same parameter data and the same SequenceNumber is sent within
> 30 minutes it will be considered a duplicate request and the sale will not process."

Sandbox-verified 2026-08-19: dedupe fires only when OrderNumber, SequenceNumber and amount
all match, and the reply is the original transaction rather than an error. The window is 30
minutes, so this is not replay protection — see
`Laravel/src/Port/OmnipayCreatePort.php`.

## Nuvei — verified from docs.nuvei.com on 2026-08-20

**`userTokenId`** — assigned by the merchant, not by Nuvei.

> "This ID uniquely identifies your consumer/user in your system. It is REQUIRED only if you
> wish to use the userPaymentOptionId parameter for future charging of this user without
> re-collecting the payment details."

The docs do **not** state what happens to stored `userPaymentOptionId` values if the token
changes. A3 must not assume they survive.

`firstName`, `lastName`, `countryCode` are required on customer creation — this is why
`CreateCustomerRequest.php:41-44` has `'N/A'` / `'US'` defaults.

## Stripe — from this repository's own code, not re-read from docs

A `Customer` is required for a `PaymentMethod` to be reusable; an unattached PM is spent by
the first confirm and refused afterwards. Established while fixing
`CreatePaymentMethodRequest` on 2026-08-06 and recorded in its docblock. `customers.create`
requires no field at all, which is why the email gate that used to guard it was removable.

**Not verified for this plan:** whether Stripe's Customer object has constraints that would
refuse an identity the aggregate considers valid. Check before F4 rather than assuming.
